WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.340
(upbeat techno music)

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:06.690
- Matte black glass, aluminum
rails, massive specs,

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:09.453
quad cameras, a hidden stylus,

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:12.210
oh wait, wait, hang on a sec.

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:14.100
Yeah, no, that was the wrong phone, sorry.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.565
Let's start that over.

00:00:15.565 --> 00:00:16.860
(upbeat techno music)

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.710
Matte black glass, aluminum rails,

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:23.913
massive specs, quad
cameras, a hidden stylus.

00:00:24.835 --> 00:00:26.348
You get the plan.

00:00:26.348 --> 00:00:29.970
(upbeat techno music continues)

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.260
Hey, what's up, MKBHD here,

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:35.880
and this is the Samsung Galaxy S23 Ultra.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.610
So, when this first came
out, when it got revealed,

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.350
it was the easiest thing to do

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:42.960
to just write it off as
an incremental upgrade,

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:44.790
because I mean, look at it.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:47.400
Aesthetically speaking, it's
basically the same phone.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.560
The side radii are squared off more,

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:51.690
so it feels a bit better
in the hand, sure,

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:53.640
much more boxy like the notes of the past.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.640
They're also slightly bigger
rings around the cameras,

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.910
and it's Gorilla Glass Victus
2 instead of Victus Plus,

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:03.810
but as far as size, industrial
design, button placement,

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:06.810
ports, the layout, it's
basically the same phone.

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:09.750
But there are two real
upgrades to this phone.

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:13.110
Now keep in mind, this is
replacing the Galaxy S22 Ultra,

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:16.590
which was already my best
big phone of the year

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:18.750
from last year, great battery,

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:20.190
great screen, great performance,

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:21.690
all of it was rock solid across the board,

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:24.600
so there's not a lot that I
would naturally want to change.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.100
But, there are two things,

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.930
and they're two of arguably
the most important things

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:29.700
you can actually change in a phone,

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:32.130
the chip that runs it all and the cameras.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.740
So you might have heard
about the Snapdragon 8 Gen 2.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.600
It's been a really good chip

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:37.980
in the other phones that it's been in,

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:40.230
excellent CPU and GPU performance

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:43.020
and really efficient which
touches battery life.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:46.140
Now, this phone, actually
the whole S23 lineup,

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:50.010
has a Snapdragon 8 Gen 2 for Galaxy,

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:52.230
a customized version of the chip,

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:54.270
specifically for these Samsung phones.

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:55.530
So if you watched the last video

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:57.150
about how Apple's taking back the iPhone,

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.130
then you know already that optimization

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:01.046
and customization for parts inside phones

00:02:01.046 --> 00:02:03.510
is a good thing, generally.

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:04.980
But the only thing that we've really seen

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:08.460
that is customized for
this chip for Galaxy

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.970
is a slightly higher max clock
speed on the performance core

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:14.010
and slightly higher
clock speed on the GPU.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:18.210
So to be exact, 3.36GHz instead of 3.2

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:23.210
on the performance core and
719MHz versus 680 on the GPU.

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:26.940
So yeah, it does score
slightly better on benchmarks

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:29.520
than the regular Snapdragon
8 Gen 2, and that's nice

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.980
for a little extra headroom
for high performance stuff,

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:33.990
light gaming and for future-proofing,

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:34.830
but that's not the whole story.

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:36.390
There's two main things that matter here,

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:38.550
one is efficiency gains.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:40.350
So, obviously performance is awesome,

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:42.270
but because efficiency is better,

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:45.360
these phones get some
serious battery life gains

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:46.890
that we'll talk in a second.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:50.124
But also too, is bye-bye Exynos,

00:02:50.124 --> 00:02:52.830
because they're not making an
Exynos version of this phone

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:54.030
as far as I can tell anywhere else.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:57.090
They're shipping every S23
Ultra with a Qualcomm chip,

00:02:57.090 --> 00:02:58.890
so everyone gets the efficiency

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:01.200
and performance gains
from the Qualcomm version.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.420
So lemme tell you, the
battery life on this phone

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:05.640
is actually, it's been incredible,

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:07.440
like it's really, really good.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.660
So it's the 5,000 million power cell again

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:12.420
shouldn't be a surprise,
but with this huge screen,

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.040
I guess it kind of is actually a surprise.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:17.820
I had a two-day period at 120Hz but 1080P,

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:20.193
where the only time I charged it

00:03:20.193 --> 00:03:22.620
was on the wireless charger in my car

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:24.240
on the way to and from the studio

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:25.770
for like the 40 minutes
that that drive is.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:27.600
I didn't charge it overnight
or anything like that.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:30.480
Two full packed days of high brightness,

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.090
high intensity, normal use for me,

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:36.118
has something like eight and a
half hours of screen-on time.

00:03:36.118 --> 00:03:40.590
I'm in bed at like 11:00 PM
at the end of the second day

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:42.150
streaming on YouTube live

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:44.340
watching LeBron break Kareem's record,

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:47.190
it's still got like 10%
left, it just won't die.

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:49.050
So combine this excellent battery life

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:51.300
with a pretty solid 45 watt charging

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:55.170
that can go zero to 100 in an
hour, plus wireless charging,

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:58.560
and you've got yourself a
battery monster, it's super good.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:03:59.610
I don't think enough people are talking

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:01.320
about how much better the battery got.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:03.990
Maybe someone will do one of
those crazy long runtime demos

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:07.200
versus the past phone, but
yeah, it's really good,

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.250
probably better than you think.

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:11.280
You kind of don't ever
need to switch to 1080P

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.110
to save batteries, matter of fact,

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:14.400
when you take it out of the box,

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:18.000
immediately just go in
and switch it to 1440P,

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.470
'cause you spent 1200 bucks on this phone,

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:21.871
and it lasts forever, treat yourself.

00:04:21.871 --> 00:04:24.510
Okay anyway, that's the chips,
that's what that enables,

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:26.100
but there's also a new set of cameras,

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:28.350
hardware and software across the board

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:30.900
that also is better than you think.

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:33.270
Now, the fundamentals are mostly the same,

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:35.190
which is why this
probably gets written off

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:36.360
so quickly a lot.

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:39.090
The layout, the aesthetics,
the focal lengths,

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:41.310
the arrangement, it's
all practically the same,

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:44.790
but we have a new
200-megapixel primary camera

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:48.330
with double the optical image
stabilization range as before.

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:49.710
That's hugely important.

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:51.810
And then new sensors
across the ultra wide,

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:54.630
the 3X telephoto, and the
10X periscope cameras.

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:56.340
This new primary sensor setup though,

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:58.890
I know we keep saying
cameras are mostly software,

00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:02.070
and as far as the look
and style of the photos,

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:04.470
it absolutely still
is, but the improvement

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.350
to the stabilization is so important here.

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:09.210
So when you go from a normal sensor

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:12.540
to a super-high resolution
200-megapixel sensor,

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.490
the fact is, in these
tiny smartphone cameras,

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:18.840
the individual pixels are
so small that individually,

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:21.570
they physically can't
bring in that much light.

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:23.820
So the camera does this
thing called binning,

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:25.350
where it combines the information

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:27.210
from a bunch of adjacent pixels

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:30.660
to form larger more accurate
pixels in your image.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:33.150
So you're not shooting
200 megapixels by default,

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:36.540
it's actually binning 16 pixels into one,

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:39.150
so you end up taking a 12.5 megapixel shot

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:41.160
for normal photos, but each photo

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:43.530
is theoretically more
accurate thanks to its makeup.

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:45.750
And then like I said, the
stabilization performance

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:48.781
on this new primary camera has doubled.

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:49.614
(phone rattles)

00:05:49.614 --> 00:05:52.290
Still rattles a little bit,
but that means it'll correct

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:55.770
up to three degrees of shake
now versus the 1.5 from before,

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:59.100
so here's an example of what's happening.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:05:59.933
If you get a lens

00:05:59.933 --> 00:06:01.729
with really good optical
image stabilization,

00:06:01.729 --> 00:06:03.660
(lens rattles) like this one,

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:06.600
that means it can
correct from the movement

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:08.550
in your hand much more,

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:12.960
which means you can hold the
camera stable for much longer,

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:14.820
so it can leave the shutter open

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:18.270
to collect more light and
still get a sharp photo.

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:22.683
So, all of this is to say
Galaxy S23 Ultra photos,

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:25.830
most of the time, in most lighting,

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:27.270
look pretty similar to last year.

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:28.260
So if that's all you're looking at,

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:30.810
just normal side by sides,
this is mostly gonna come down

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:32.460
to the different software tuning,

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:34.920
and there's a little bit more
dynamic range than last year,

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:36.570
but yeah, still top of the line

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:39.270
while mostly avoiding looking to HDR-y.

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:42.300
Photos are typically pretty
warm from these Samsung phones,

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:44.130
and they have a slightly punchier,

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:46.020
more contrasty look than before,

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:47.730
still very much up the Samsung alley

00:06:47.730 --> 00:06:50.220
of colorful and saturated,
but it's an aesthetic

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:52.410
that I can get behind, I really like.

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:55.110
But, on top of that,
having this new sensor

00:06:55.110 --> 00:06:57.780
and optical stabilization means one,

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:01.290
you can shoot literally
200-megapixel photos now

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:02.700
if you really want to.

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:05.100
Now, this does accomplish
the intended purpose

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:08.370
of capturing much more of the finer detail

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:09.540
in things like landscapes,

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:11.520
so if you plan on zooming
in on the shot later,

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:13.110
or if you're one of the
three people on earth

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:15.510
who will actually print
a smartphone photo,

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:17.550
this should work, but
you should also be aware

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:18.810
that it's only really able

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:21.330
to give you these types of
results in excellent lighting

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:22.200
where a ton of light

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:24.750
is hitting every individual little pixel.

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:25.920
Anything short of that,

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:28.110
and you're gonna get a
lot of noise really quick.

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:30.660
And there's also a
really solid shutter lag

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:33.921
as it turns out these massive
40, 50 megabyte files,

00:07:33.921 --> 00:07:37.290
granted this mode is mostly
for things sitting still,

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:39.810
like a landscape or a photo
shoot but worth noting.

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:41.040
I think the better compromise

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:44.700
is you actually also
get a 50-megapixel mode,

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:47.250
which kicks out still very detailed images

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:50.640
that hang right with the iPhone's
48-megapixel ProRAW shots

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:53.520
in a variety of light, but now
the files are five megabytes,

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:55.050
and there's a lot of less shutter lag.

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:56.460
But there's still that improved detail

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:58.560
over the normal binge shots
and not as much noise.

00:07:58.560 --> 00:07:59.880
It's all about flexibility.

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:01.170
The standard mode is gonna be the best

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:02.550
for most shots most of the time,

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:04.290
but you can always turn
it up if you want to,

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:06.180
and that's very much the
same thing with the zoom.

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:07.440
You see all the cameras on the back.

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:10.260
Any phone with two
different telephoto cameras

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:13.230
is gonna have the biggest
range of good zoom performance.

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:14.840
On this phone, anything past 10X

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:17.040
is where it really shines
compared to others.

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:18.450
And you might have even
seen my recent clip

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:21.060
of taking a photo of
the full moon recently,

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:24.780
which seems to blow people's
minds every time they see it.

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:27.720
Wow, but you also can't
forget about video too.

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:29.970
This is improved video across the board

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:32.430
with better processing, the new sensors,

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:36.540
and the much better stabilization,
thanks to the better OIS.

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:39.480
So this might be the
best super steady mode

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:41.790
I've ever seen in smartphone video,

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:44.910
and the beauty of it being
from optical stabilization

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:46.740
is it works great in
a variety of lighting,

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:49.350
unlike some electronic
image stabilization,

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:50.910
which relies on having a ton of light.

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:52.560
And on top of all of that,

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:56.833
the 8K video on this
smartphone is very usable.

00:08:56.833 --> 00:08:58.980
There are previous phones
that have had 8K video,

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:00.180
it's not the first,

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:02.580
but I remember when they
first got that capability,

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:04.470
they'd always be at like 24 FPS,

00:09:04.470 --> 00:09:06.120
'cause that's the most
that they could churn out,

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:10.980
which is not the right frame
rate, so 8K/30 really good.

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:12.480
And if you put it
side-by-side with the 4K,

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:14.280
you can actually see
the sharpness difference

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:15.420
if you really punch in.

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:16.770
If you want a sample of this,

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:19.320
the latest Auto Focus
video I shot in my car

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:21.210
is in 8K from this phone,

00:09:21.210 --> 00:09:23.970
and you can actually go watch
it 8K on YouTube right now

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:26.580
from the link below, hit that
like button if you want to.

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:27.413
Oh yeah, and also,

00:09:27.413 --> 00:09:29.430
don't forget about the better selfies too.

00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:31.950
There's a new 12 megapixel selfie camera

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:33.260
in all these S23 phones.

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:36.420
And while that number is lower on paper

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:38.130
than the 40 megapixel selfie camera

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:41.089
that came before it, it's better.

00:09:41.089 --> 00:09:43.200
It's just better, rock solid proof

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:44.910
that the megapixels don't matter.

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:47.640
This selfie camera, with the
better software processing,

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:50.790
is very sharp, detailed, has nice color,

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:53.610
doesn't flare too much, and
also has a decently wide angle.

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:55.260
It's not ultra-wide but not bad.

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:58.290
So across the board, this is significant,

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:00.390
an extensive improvement to the camera,

00:10:00.390 --> 00:10:01.920
especially the primary camera.

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:03.510
That feels overlooked to me

00:10:03.510 --> 00:10:05.257
when people have been reviewing the phone.

00:10:05.257 --> 00:10:07.920
The one thing I still will complain about

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:09.630
is there is still shutter lag,

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:12.240
which is different from
slow shutter speed.

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:14.730
So the time gap between
hitting the shutter button

00:10:14.730 --> 00:10:17.670
and actually capturing the
photo, it's still real,

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:18.810
and it can still be kind of annoying,

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:21.780
even if you capture a crisp
photo of the wrong moment.

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:23.670
So, like I said, it's more pronounced

00:10:23.670 --> 00:10:26.040
when you take the ultra
high resolution 50-megapixel

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:27.390
or 200-megapixel photos.

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:29.340
You can't exactly do those in rapid fire.

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:30.367
But if the question is,

00:10:30.367 --> 00:10:32.167
"Did they make a meaningful improvement

00:10:32.167 --> 00:10:34.252
"to last year's phone to end up here?"

00:10:34.252 --> 00:10:37.050
I would say between the new chip

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:38.640
and the better overall performance,

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:39.750
and much better efficiency,

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:42.270
which gets you huge
battery life improvement,

00:10:42.270 --> 00:10:44.760
and the new cameras
with the better sensors,

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:48.076
better processing, but also
much better stabilization,

00:10:48.076 --> 00:10:52.588
I would say yes, not upgrade
from last year's phone, yes,

00:10:52.588 --> 00:10:54.660
but they've actually
made a real improvement.

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:56.970
And then, I don't really need
to say too much about the rest

00:10:56.970 --> 00:10:59.010
because it's the same as before,

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:01.708
which, in the case of the
best big phone of last year,

00:11:01.708 --> 00:11:03.240
is kind of a good thing.

00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:05.430
All the other things that
made this the best big phone

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:08.340
are still here, and they're
not minor things either.

00:11:08.340 --> 00:11:10.950
I haven't even talked
about the A+ display,

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:15.950
1440P, 120Hz LTPO, 1,750
nits peak brightness,

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:18.900
it's still awesome,
still has great speakers,

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:20.610
still has very reliable software

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:22.560
with a pretty good track record now

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:23.850
of delivering software updates

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:26.040
in a timely fashion for a while.

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:28.530
The base storage has
also actually jumped up

00:11:28.530 --> 00:11:33.530
from 128 to 256 gigs, and it's
faster UFS 4.0 storage now.

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:37.200
It still has the best stylus
in a smartphone in the world,

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:39.240
which might mean a lot more
to you than it does to me,

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:41.220
but, honestly, if I ever use it,

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:42.870
it's nice knowing I can at any time

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:45.360
mark up a screenshot or sign a PDF.

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:47.220
And the list goes on, great haptic motor,

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:49.770
nice clicky buttons, it's all still here.

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:52.410
This thing sets the standard pretty high.

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:53.880
My analogy that I was making

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:57.600
is that it feels like the
portion 9/11 of smartphones.

00:11:57.600 --> 00:12:00.360
If you're gonna charge
1200 bucks for a phone,

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:02.550
it better set high marks all
the way across the board,

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:04.680
but it does, and it's pretty underrated,

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:06.570
kind of boring, but it does.

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:08.070
Now, if you want the S23 Ultra

00:12:08.070 --> 00:12:11.190
to look as improved as it actually is,

00:12:11.190 --> 00:12:13.380
I would recommend a skin from
channel sponsored, dbrand,

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:15.330
maybe something like this Damascus skin,

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:16.530
which adds a lot of character,

00:12:16.530 --> 00:12:19.140
where it would ordinarily be pretty blank.

00:12:19.140 --> 00:12:20.430
My favorite one is the Triple Black.

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:21.690
It is actually included for free

00:12:21.690 --> 00:12:23.940
when you pick up any of
the holographic colorways,

00:12:23.940 --> 00:12:26.220
so you can check 'em
out at the link below.

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:27.480
I say this phone is boring,

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:30.607
and I think maybe understated
is the better word.

00:12:30.607 --> 00:12:33.300
Are there gonna be other
phones that come out this year

00:12:33.300 --> 00:12:37.249
that do one up this phone in
certain single categories?

00:12:37.249 --> 00:12:39.840
Yeah, 100%, there's probably gonna be

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:42.330
a phone with 120X zoom.

00:12:42.330 --> 00:12:46.140
There's probably gonna be a
phone with crazy fast charging.

00:12:46.140 --> 00:12:48.900
This is only 45 watt charging.
Do I wish this was better?

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:50.160
A little bit, sometimes.

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:51.180
Is there gonna be a phone probably

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:53.590
with a much bigger, better,
faster fingerprint reader?

00:12:53.590 --> 00:12:55.137
(soft bright music)
Yeah, probably.

00:12:55.137 --> 00:12:58.410
But as far as just nailing all
the marks across the board,

00:12:58.410 --> 00:12:59.250
yeah, this does it.

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:00.600
Just as far as overall package,

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:05.070
Samsung's software is settled,
the screen is sublime,

00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:07.080
it's still the sickest stylus,

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:10.893
and it's snaps significantly
smoother shots, sick.

00:13:11.776 --> 00:13:15.809
Thanks for watching, catch you
guys in the next one, peace.

00:13:15.809 --> 00:13:19.226
(bright music continues)

